+## #203 — check-retired-apps.mjs fails 19 times — **FIXED & CLOSED**
+
+**Problem:** The retired-apps check failed 19 times at the promoted main head. 17 were false positives (the checker matched the bare product name "Borys", which is also an ordinary given name). 1 was a real reference (a comment in keys.ts referencing `source/borys/docs/API.md`).
+
+**Fix:**
+1. `scripts/check-retired-apps.mjs`: Match retired apps by handles (appPath, route, namespace in route form) instead of bare product name. (Already on release line at `86dd8002`.)
+2. `source/kawunapp/src/backend/capstore/core/keys.ts`: Removed the parenthetical reference to `source/borys/docs/API.md` from a comment.
+
+**Landed:** `a30afa45` on `origin/main`.
+
+**Verification:**
+- `node scripts/check-retired-apps.mjs` passes: 1259 files scanned, 0 failures
+- `npm run check` passes: lint, rules:test 3/3, test 413 files/1367 tests, filesystem policy, locked policy unchanged
+
+**Board:** Comment added, issue closed.
+
+## #155 — user/module grants and owner capability recovery — **BLOCKED**
+
+**Status:** Implementation verified resolved on `origin/main` (commits `5b3a5cca`/`371f7848`, 1367 tests pass). But the issue carries a recorded request-changes review blocker (`cd5b5be90e71`) against residual C.
+
+**Residual C:** `tools/eslint-plugin-kawun/rules/directory-imports.js` covers `ImportDeclaration` but not `ImportExpression` (dynamic `import()`). A second authority axis is reachable from production code with all gates green. Closing this requires modifying a hash-locked rule file — an authorized policy change reserved for the Founder.
+
+**Next:** Await Founder decision on the locked-policy change. No duplicate work spawned.
+
+## #195 — Single-holder landing queue — **BLOCKED**
+
+**Status:** 14 commits on `origin/release/along-long-namespace` @ `985c6638`. Landing onto main is barred by the same residual C issue as #155.
+
+**Next:** Await Founder decision on the locked-policy change. Ready to land immediately when the policy gate is resolved.
+
+## Other Kawun work
+
+No other Kawun issues are open on the Antonina board. The skrynia-apps feature backlog (#13–39) is not on the board and is not being executed.
+
